UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482532
DESCRIPTION:# InventOR Bootcamp Mentor &amp\; Judge Opportunities | Suppo
 rt Oregon Student Innovators&#13\;\n&#13\;\n&#13\;\nJoin the PSU Center 
 for Entrepreneurship (https://www.pdx.edu/entrepreneurship/) in supporti
 ng the **10th Annual InventOR**\, Oregon’s only statewide collegiate inv
 ention competition.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nInventOR (https://www.inventoregon.or
 g/) is an 8-week experiential program that helps collegiate inventors an
 d innovators refine their ideas through mentorship\, prototyping\, story
 telling\, and exposure to Oregon’s startup ecosystem.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nWe 
 are expanding our mentor and judge network and invite professionals from
  across industries to participate in one (or both) of the following **In
 ventOR Bootcamp** opportunities:&#13\;\n&#13\;\n---&#13\;\n&#13\;\n## Me
 ntor Match Mixer  &#13\;\n**Saturday\, May 2 | 6:00–8:00 PM**  &#13\;\n*
 *SEC Event Space\, Portland State University**  &#13\;\n2130 SW 5th Ave\
 , Portland\, OR 97201  &#13\;\n&#13\;\nA speed-networking style event wh
 ere student finalist teams and prospective mentors meet to explore mento
 rship fit.&#13\;\n&#13\;\n### How it Works&#13\;\n- ~20 student finalist
  teams participate  &#13\;\n- Teams give a 60-second overview of their p
 roject  &#13\;\n- Mentors give a 60-second intro/background  &#13\;\n- B
 rief Q&amp\;A / discussion  &#13\;\n- Participants rotate through multip
 le pairings  &#13\;\n&#13\;\n### Important&#13\;\nMentor matches are mad
 e **after the event** based on **mutual interest and fit**.  &#13\;\n*At
 tendance does not guarantee a mentor assignment.*&#13\;\n&#13\;\nMatched
  mentors receive a **$500 honorarium** for:&#13\;\n&#13\;\n- Meeting wit
 h their team at least twice during the 8-week program  &#13\;\n- Providi
 ng strategic guidance and feedback  &#13\;\n- Virtual/Zoom meetings are 
 welcome  &#13\;\n&#13\;\n---&#13\;\n&#13\;\n## Pitch for Feedback Judge 
 Session  &#13\;\n**Sunday\, May 3 | 9:00 AM–12:00 PM**  &#13\;\n**Embass
 y Suites\, Downtown Portland**&#13\;\n&#13\;\nHelp teams prepare for Inv
 entOR Finals by serving as a practice pitch judge.&#13\;\n&#13\;\n### Ju
 dges Will&#13\;\n- Listen to 3-minute student pitches  &#13\;\n- Ask fol
 low-up questions  &#13\;\n- Provide written feedback  &#13\;\n- Offer re
 commendations on design\, strategy\, and next steps  &#13\;\n&#13\;\n---
 &#13\;\n&#13\;\n## Interested?&#13\;\n&#13\;\nPlease fill out our Mentor
 /Judge Interest Form:  &#13\;\n[Get Involved: Support the Next Generatio
 n of Innovators!](https://airtable.com/appVhNsjzbDOfUJDp/pagvuCPqqS9ETDn
 xg/form)&#13\;\n&#13\;\nThen email Stacey Hoshimiya at [s.hoshimiya@pdx.
 edu](mailto:s.hoshimiya@pdx.edu) to confirm your participation at one or
  both Bootcamp events.&#13\;\n&#13\;\n---&#13\;\n&#13\;\nHelp us support
  the next generation of Oregon innovators!&#13\;\n&#13\;\n\n\nTags: #sud
 ententreprenueurs\, #centerforentrepreneurship\, #PSU\, #InventOR\, #inn
 ovation\, #changemakers\, #entrepreneurship\, #Startups\n\nImported from
 : http://calagator.org/events/1250482532
URL:https://www.inventoregon.org/
SUMMARY:InventOR Bootcamp Mentor & Judge Opportunities | Support Oregon S
 tudent Innovators
LOCATION:SEC Event Space: 2130 SW 5th Ave\, Portland OR 97201 United Stat
 es
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
