BEGIN:VEVENT
CREATED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T165614Z
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260514T190000
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260514T173000
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T165614Z
LAST-MODIFIED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T165614Z
UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482543
DESCRIPTION:This presentation introduces D3.js as a powerful tool for tra
 nsforming complex data into clear\, meaningful visual stories which non-
 technical audiences can understand and use. It explains what D3.js is\, 
 how it works with web technologies and why visualization is essential fo
 r revealing patterns and insights raw data alone cannot show.&#13\;\n&#1
 3\;\nThis talk emphasizes designing visualizations with the audience in 
 mind while also covering core D3 concepts such as data binding\, scales\
 , layouts and interactive graphics. Through examples\, case studies\, de
 sign principles and practical tips\, this presentation demonstrates how 
 builders can use D3.js to communicate ideas effectively and empower peop
 le to discover insights from data.\n\nTags: portland design thinkers\, d
 ata visualizations\, UX research\, problem solving\, collaboration\, inn
 ovation\n\nImported from: http://calagator.org/events/1250482543
URL:https://www.meetup.com/portland-design-thinkers/events/314420080/
SUMMARY:Building D3.js Visualizations For Non-Technical Audiences
LOCATION:Virtual: false
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CREATED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260430T222445Z
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260514T193000
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260514T173000
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260430T222445Z
LAST-MODIFIED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260430T222445Z
UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482554
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Native PDX May: Change-driven Architecture and Serving 
 Inference at Scale&#13\;\n&#13\;\nThis May is all about scaling\; scalin
 g your infrastructure management\, or scaling your LLM inference serving
 . Join us to find out about some open source tools to make managing larg
 e modern stacks easier.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nDate: Thursday\, May 14&#13\;\nTi
 me: 5:30–7:30 PM&#13\;\nLocation: Reperio Health\, 4784 SE 17th Ave Suit
 e 120\, Portland\, OR&#13\;\n&#13\;\nRecording: Talks are typically reco
 rded (opt-in by speakers)&#13\;\n&#13\;\nA big thank you to Microsoft fo
 r sponsoring food &amp\; beverage\, and to Reperio Health\, our venue ho
 st.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nDrasi\, a new take on Change Driven Architectures: Am
 an Singh\, Microsoft&#13\;\n&#13\;\nModern cloud-native systems constant
 ly generate data changes\, and applications often need to react to them.
  Building change-driven solutions that respond to specific changes in di
 stributed data is challenging. This talk introduces Drasi\, a CNCF Sandb
 ox project that simplifies the design and implementation of change-drive
 n architectures using Graph Queries and pluggable components. For exampl
 e\, with Drasi you can declaratively write automation to detect and resp
 ond to running containers with newly identified vulnerabilities across p
 ods and deployments in a Kubernetes cluster. Join us for a walkthrough o
 f real-world use cases that show how Drasi’s approach brings structure a
 nd responsiveness to complex distributed environments - without writing 
 custom code.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nDynamo: Large Scale Distributed Inference&#1
 3\;\nDavid Zeir\, Director\, DL System Software\, Nvidia&#13\;\nNeelay S
 hah\, Distinguished Engineer\, Nvidia&#13\;\n&#13\;\nThis talk introduce
 s Dynamo\, NVIDIA's open-source Kubernetes-native distributed inference 
 platform. We'll cover the problem space\, walk through Dynamo's architec
 ture — disaggregated prefill/decode\, KV-cache-aware routing\, and a tra
 nsport layer that moves KV blocks directly between GPUs — and dig into t
 he Kubernetes integration for scheduling\, autoscaling\, and graceful fa
 ilure handling. We'll close with a demo of Dynamo serving a real workloa
 d.\n\nTags: kubernetes\, containers\, cloud\, intrastructure\, devops\, 
 LLM\, inference\n\nImported from: http://calagator.org/events/1250482554
URL:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-native-pdx/events/314391212
SUMMARY:Cloud Native May Meetup: Change-driven Architecture and Serving I
 nference at Scale
LOCATION:Reperio Health: 4784 SE 17th Ave Suite 120\, Portland OR 97202 U
 SA
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
